{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"771","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Bear and Different Names"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the army, it isn't easy to form a group of soldiers that will be effective on the battlefield. The communication is crucial and thus no two soldiers should share a name (what would happen if they got an order that Bob is a scouter, if there are two Bobs?)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A group of soldiers is effective if and only if their names are different. For example, a group (John, Bob, Limak) would be effective, while groups (Gary, Bob, Gary) and (Alice, Alice) wouldn't."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are a spy in the enemy's camp. You noticed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" soldiers standing in a row, numbered "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". The general wants to choose a group of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" consecutive soldiers. For every "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" consecutive soldiers, the general wrote down whether they would be an effective group or not."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You managed to steal the general's notes, with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - k + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" strings "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s1, s2, ..., sn - k + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":", each either \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s1"},{"kind":"text","text":" describes a group of soldiers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" (\""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if the group is effective, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise). "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" The string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s2"},{"kind":"text","text":" describes a group of soldiers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" And so on, till the string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"sn - k + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" that describes a group of soldiers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - k + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to find possible names of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" soldiers. Names should match the stolen notes. Each name should be a string that consists of between "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"10"},{"kind":"text","text":" English letters, inclusive. The first letter should be uppercase, and all other letters should be lowercase. Names don't have to be existing names — it's allowed to print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Xyzzzdj"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"T"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" for example."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find and print any solution. It can be proved that there always exists at least one solution."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ k ≤ n ≤ 50"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of soldiers and the size of a group respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n - k + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" strings "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"s1, s2, ..., sn - k + 1"},{"kind":"text","text":". The string "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"si"},{"kind":"text","text":" is \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if the group of soldiers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i + k - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":" is effective, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Find any solution satisfying all given conditions. In one line print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":